# Type Safety Mandate

## Core Requirements
- Zero `any` types allowed
- Define interfaces for all API payloads and DB records
- Validate runtime data with Zod or similar validation libraries

## Type Definitions
- Database Types: [src/integrations/supabase/types.ts](mdc:src/integrations/supabase/types.ts)
- Environment Types: [src/types/environment.d.ts](mdc:src/types/environment.d.ts)

## Type Safety Rules
1. Use TypeScript strict mode
2. Define explicit return types for functions
3. Avoid type assertions unless absolutely necessary
4. Use generics for reusable components/functions
5. Define proper types for async operations

## Runtime Validation
- Validate all API responses
- Type check all external data
- Ensure proper error handling for type mismatches

## Examples
- Supabase Client: [src/integrations/supabase/client.ts](mdc:src/integrations/supabase/client.ts)
- Config Types: [src/lib/config.ts](mdc:src/lib/config.ts)

